<%# An empty list is not a gap in the page: chapter 3.2.4 has a member state
    declare `NoMatch` to say it knows it issues nothing under this
    jurisdiction, where `EB:ERR:0001` would mean the broker holds nothing at
    all. The reason it may attach is what lets a reader look elsewhere. %>
<li class="entry <%= 'entry--grouped' if local_assigns[:grouped] %>">
  <span class="entry__name"><%= t('admin.common_services.no_match.declared') %></span>
  <%# The reason travels in the member state's own language — the chapter has
      them write it in a widely understood one, so rarely French — and the
      passage carries it, failing which a screen reader reads English aloud in
      French (RGAA 8.7). Omitted rather than left empty where the directory
      published no `lang`. `R-EB-EVI-C045` makes the attribute mandatory and
      names `EN` as its default, but that default is the publisher's to apply:
      a directory that dropped it may as well have published French, and
      declaring a language we do not know is how a screen reader is made to
      mispronounce confidently. %>
  <% if list.match_description.present? %>
    <%= tag.span(list.match_description, class: 'fr-hint-text',
          lang: list.match_description_language&.downcase.presence) %>
  <% end %>
</li>
